<v David Kestenbaum>Tim looked around at similar companies, some in the same industry, some in the same geographic area. And he couldn't find any where the CEO was paid even half of what Horowitz made. Now, if you just own a few shares of a company's stock and you think the CEO is overpaid, there isn't much you can do. But if you own more, well, that's different. And by the fall of 2009, Tim owned 180,000 shares.
<v David Kestenbaum>蒂姆环顾类似的公司，一些在同一个行业，一些在同一个地理区域。他找不到任何一家公司首席执行官的薪水是霍洛维茨的一半。现在，如果你只拥有公司的一点股票，而你认为首席执行官报酬过高，你做不了什么。但如果你拥有更多，好吧，那就不同了。到2009年秋天，蒂姆拥有18万股股份。

