<v Andrew Shapiro>I'm Andrew Shapiro. I'm president and portfolio manager of Lawndale Capital Management.
<v Andrew Shapiro>我是安德鲁·夏皮罗（Andrew Shapiro）。我是Lawndale Capital Management的总裁和投资组合经理。

00:40:12.230 --> 00:40:25.430
<v David Kestenbaum>Andrew also owned a big chunk of the company, about 8%. He and Tim didn't work together directly. They had very different styles. Andrew was a by-the-book investor, fond of semi-obscure military allusions.
<v David Kestenbaum>安德鲁也拥有该公司的一大块股份，大约8%。他和蒂姆没有直接合作。他们有非常不同的风格。安德鲁是一位循规蹈矩的投资者，喜欢半晦涩的军事典故。

00:40:25.430 --> 00:40:36.110
<v Andrew Shapiro>With what we do, we deploy what I call the Powell Doctrine of investments. And I try to take on targets where I can mount overwhelming force.
<v Andrew Shapiro>通过我们的工作，我们部署了我称之为投资的“鲍威尔主义”（Powell Doctrine）。我尝试承担目标，在那里我可以施加压倒性的力量。

00:40:36.110 --> 00:40:50.000
<v Jacob Goldstein>For years, Andrew had been arguing that the CEO was grossly overpaid. Over one 10-year period, he says, Richard Horowitz took home $13.5 million dollars. That's more than twice what the entire company made in profits over that time.
<v Jacob Goldstein>多年来，安德鲁一直在争论首席执行官的报酬严重过高。他说，在一段10年期间，理查德·霍洛维茨带回家1350万美元。这超过了整个公司在那段时间所赚利润的两倍。

00:40:50.000 --> 00:41:05.580
<v David Kestenbaum>Sometimes, when people complain about CEO pay, they talk about it as if the money's coming out of the pockets of ordinary workers. That is not how Tim and Andrew see it. Every dollar the CEO gets is $1 less profit, $1 less for Tim and Andrew and all the other stockholders.
<v David Kestenbaum>有时，当人们抱怨首席执行官薪酬时，他们谈论它好像钱是从普通工人的口袋里掏出来的一样。那不是蒂姆和安德鲁看待它的方式。首席执行官得到的每一美元都是利润少了一美元，对蒂姆、安德鲁和所有其他股东来说少了一美元。

00:41:05.580 --> 00:41:09.080
<v Andrew Shapiro>The overpaid CEO's taking money out of the shareowner's pocket.
<v Andrew Shapiro>报酬过高的首席执行官正从股东的口袋里拿钱。

00:41:09.080 --> 00:41:16.100
<v David Kestenbaum>You're not in it because, hey, wouldn't it feel great if CEOs weren't paid so much more than everyone else?
<v David Kestenbaum>你不是为了，嘿，如果首席执行官的薪水没有比其他人高那么多，那感觉不是很好吗？

