<v Andrew Shapiro>I am doing this to make a return on our capital.
<v Andrew Shapiro>我做这件事是为了从我们的资本中获得回报。

00:41:20.690 --> 00:41:42.940
<v Jacob Goldstein>This is why, if you think CEOs are overpaid rich guys, your best hope for changing things may be other rich guys, rich guys with enough money to buy up a bunch of stock and take on the company to try and cut the CEO's pay, in hopes of becoming even richer themselves.
<v Jacob Goldstein>这就是为什么，如果你认为首席执行官是报酬过高的有钱人，你改变现状的最好希望可能是其他有钱人，那些有足够钱购买一堆股票并承担公司试图削减首席执行官薪水、希望让自己变得更富有的有钱人。

00:41:42.940 --> 00:42:02.810
<v David Kestenbaum>We, of course, wanted to know what the CEO Richard Horowitz had to say about this. We tried to get him. We had a bunch of talks with the company's lawyer. In the end, Horowitz declined to be interviewed. But because this is a public company, there are plenty of recordings of him. Public companies have what are called "quarterly earnings calls" for investors, really anyone who wants to listen.
<v David Kestenbaum>我们当然想知道首席执行官理查德·霍洛维茨对此有什么看法。我们试图联系他。我们和公司的律师进行了多次谈话。最后，霍洛维茨拒绝接受采访。但因为这是一间上市公司，有很多关于他的录音。上市公司有所谓的针对投资者的“季度收益电话”，实际上任何想听的人都可以听。

